@baseUrl = http://localhost:4001/api
@accessToken = paste-access-token-here
@refreshToken = paste-refresh-token-here

### Manual examples only. Send requests individually against the intended environment.
### POST registration sends email and creates data; agreement must reflect the user's action.
### Do not run these write requests as passive health checks.

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Browse schools
GET {{baseUrl}}/schools?search=technology&maxTuition=70000&sort=rating

### Register - check the user's email for the verification code
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student@example.com",
  "password": "StrongPass123!",
  "confirmPassword": "StrongPass123!",
  "firstName": "Sample",
  "middleName": "",
  "lastName": "Student",
  "address": "Taguig City",
  "acceptedPolicies": true,
  "policyVersion": "2026-10-20-v2"
}

### Verify email
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student@example.com",
  "code": "paste-code-here"
}

### Login - copy accessToken and refreshToken to the variables above
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student@example.com",
  "password": "StrongPass123!"
}

### Get assessment questions
GET {{baseUrl}}/assessments/questions

### Own saved assessment history - read only
GET {{baseUrl}}/assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Assessment submission is intentionally not hard-coded here.
### GET questions, retain version/workflow, collect every actual question/option ID,
### POST /assessments/routing, then complete the returned follow-ups before final POST.
### See docs/api-reference.md for the versioned payload. Final submission consumes
### the default one-time attempt; do not use it as a production health probe.

### Dashboard
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Own profile - do not publish returned home coordinates or other personal data
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Collection summary - read only, does not run scraping
GET {{baseUrl}}/catalog/status

### Administrator source summary - authorized admin token required, read only
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/scraping
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
